# DALALAH — environment variables
#
# This prototype is a fully static, self-contained site. It stores all
# demo data (listings, favorites, drafts) in the visitor's browser via
# localStorage and does not call any backend API, so no environment
# variables or API keys are required to run or deploy it.
#
# This file is included only to satisfy tooling that expects a
# .env.example to exist. There is nothing to fill in today.
#
# If you later connect a real backend (e.g. Supabase) for auth,
# storage, and a shared database, you would add variables such as:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
